          "pause": true,
          "displayType": "poster",
          "buttonOnMobile": false,
          "label": "<p>In the second case, a 3-year-old boy has had fever for six days with bilateral r</p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>In the second case, a 3-year-old boy has had fever for six days with bilateral red eyes (no discharge), cracked red lips, puffy red hands, and a tender cervical lymph node. Which organ is most at risk if treatment is delayed beyond the ten-day window?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Lungs</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Pulmonary involvement is not a primary feature of this condition. The inflammatory process targets medium-sized arteries, not the airways.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Kidneys</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Renal involvement is more characteristic of Henoch-Schönlein purpura or lupus. In this disease the primary vascular target is different.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Coronary arteries</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>This presentation is Kawasaki disease, which inflames medium-sized blood vessels — especially the coronary arteries. Every day of delayed treatment increases the risk of coronary artery aneurysms.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Brain</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>While irritability may occur, the critical target organ in Kawasaki disease is the coronary vasculature, not the central nervous system.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "The narration highlighted that every additional day of delay leaves the coronary arteries exposed to ongoing inflammation. Kawasaki disease is a medium-vessel vasculitis whose principal danger is coronary artery aneurysm formation."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Correct! Kawasaki disease threatens the coronary arteries. Treatment with intravenous immunoglobulin within the first ten days of fever dramatically reduces aneurysm risk."
                }
              ],
              "behaviour": {
